  "question": {
    "text": "A mass $\\mathrm{m}$ hangs with the help of a string wrapped around a pulley on a frictionless bearing. The pulley has mass $\\mathrm{m}$ and radius $\\mathrm{R}$. Assuming pulley to be a perfect uniform circular disc, the acceleration of the mass $m$, if the string does not slip on the pulley, is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "sf6wm",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{g}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "UAywv",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{2}{3} \\mathrm{~g}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "Yjgea",
      "text": "\n $\\frac{\\mathrm{g}}{3}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "iEJ30",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{3}{2} g$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& M g-T=M a \\quad \\quad \\ldots \\ldots (1)\\\\\n& T \\times R=I \\alpha=\\frac{1}{2} M^2 \\alpha \\\\\n& T=\\frac{1}{2} M a \\quad(a=\\alpha R) \\quad \\quad \\ldots \\ldots (2)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nFrom (1) and (2) $a=\\frac{2 g}{3}$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/iMu_Avph2shfmF7EI3FTpacRqBrMHQQAUs7TY_xP0Ho.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
